# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets — never commit. The IDE session logs contain pasted API keys.
#
# `.env.example` is carved back out: it documents what a fresh clone needs and
# holds no values. Without the exception the rule above swallows it too, so it
# gets written and then silently never committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
sess_*/

# Build / media artifacts
*.mp4
*.mp3
build/
dist/

# Except the voice previews. Those are not artifacts of a render, they are
# the catalogue: one short clip per voice, made once by
# `python -m videosynx.voice_samples`, so that choosing between fifty-four
# identifiers is something you can hear instead of guess. Four megabytes that
# do not change until a voice does.
!web/public/voices/*.mp3

# Output videos — large, and regenerable
tmp/
